      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-45269",
      ":question/problem": "Fill in the table below, and use this to find a value of $x$ that corresponds to an approximate solution of the system\n${y =-2x + 5; y = 4x + 1$.\n\n| $x$ | $0.5$ | $0.6$ | $0.7$ | $0.8$ | $0.9$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $y_{1} =-2x + 5$ | $4$ |  |  |  | $3.2$ |\n| $y_{2} = 4x + 1$ | $3$ |  |  |  | $4.6$ |\n| $\\mid y_{1} - y_{2} \\mid$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $1.4$ |\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
